Z||000000||BroCar 87||06-08-2000||05:24 PM||||Hey Guys (and girls), I was wondering if anyone knows of a good place to get a DOG BONE from. Whats the best one and where do i get it from? I have an 87 4cyl. Thanks in Advance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||LarryB||06-08-2000||05:27 PM||||The Fiero Store carries them for both 4 and 6 cyl, <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A>  and got to 4 cyl mounts in the online catalog.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||06-08-2000||09:17 PM||||NAPA Autoparts. In your neighborhood I'm sure. My V6 dogbone was $11. Not as fancy as the Fierostores Ultimate dogbone, but you could have it by Saturday.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BroCar 87||06-08-2000||09:56 PM||||Thanks Larry, Thanks Stimpy,  I have another quick question... If the ULTIMATE dog bone is $50 and the original is 11, is it worth getting the ULTIMATE and how much better is it. SUGGESTIONS ACCEPTED...lol should i go ahead and get the OEM or Ultimate? <P>GOSH....  DECISIONS DECISIONS DECISIONS  haha||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||06-08-2000||10:21 PM||||Yo, Bro!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I just got the polyurethane rebuild kit for my GT.<P>Awesome!<P>of course, I also replaced the front tranny mount at the same time... no clunk clunk.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||06-09-2000||07:32 AM||||Will the ultimate dogbone work? Of course. It will work great. But 5 times better than stock? Doubt it. It is very fancy looking and no doubt would last forever, but a stock V6 is not going to out torque a stock bone. And you can always take metal polish to the stock bone if you want fancy.<P>Not knocking the ultimate dogbone, but does a $5 roll of toilet paper clean yer azz better then a $1 roll?  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||06-09-2000||04:47 PM||||NO! But your ass-0-meter feels better with the $5 roll. HA HA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shadow Wolf||06-11-2000||03:43 AM||||Any roll of toilet paper will do the job, but would you rather use the soft stuff, or the stuff they have at gas stations?||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||06-11-2000||08:25 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||06-11-2000||08:25 AM||||The ultimate dogbone uses poly bushings and the stock one uses plain ol' rubber. Ogre and I can both tell you, if you have a 87-88 Fieros with the 2.5, don't even mess with the standard rubber one, they wear out extremely fast because there are only 2 lower mounts compared to the 3 lower mounts for the rest of the cars, so the dogbone takes a lot of abuse. Go with the poly bushings. I drove my 87 SE for 3 years and went through 2 OEM rubber dogbones. Ogre does lots of stop and go driving and wears his out even faster I think.||||reg||1
Z||000010||William||06-11-2000||09:00 AM||||Hey Brocar,<BR>You can come by and check out my Ultimate dogbone if you like. (That doesn't sound right lol). Anyway, it's the one for the v-6 but you'll get the idea. Let me know.||||reg||12
Z||000011||theogre||06-11-2000||04:05 PM||||What bat's said, 87-88 4 cyl with automatic needs poly bones. I put polly bushings into an "old style" dogbone and put that on. Cost me about $20, and keeps a stock look. I chewed thru the OEM one in about 15,000 miles, and the weak bone was resulting in damage to the exhaust and the intake. Those problems are now gone.<P>Because of the way the engine and the automatic are mounted after 86.5 you'll get a noticable increase in vibration at idle, but it goes away as soon as you start moving. One thing that helps is to knock the tranny into nuetral at long traffic lights. This unloads the drivetrain and bone which reduces the amount of vibration transmitted to the body.<P>this is only an issue for 86.5 and latter 4 cyl and automatic. On all other configurations there will be an increase in vibration but not very bad.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||BroCar 87||06-11-2000||08:33 PM||||WOW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    Thanks for the responces! I really appreciate them.  Thanks for the inside info BATBOY and THEOGRE. I do shift into nuetral at lights BECAUSE of the vibration... good to know its not just me. <BR>Well the verdict is... I get paid on tuesday, I will find out how much an O.E.M. dogbone costs from the local auto stores, and will buy one of those to tide me over until i move out. I am saving my money to finally rid my parents of myself.(moving out on my own / roommate)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>BUT AS SOON AS I MOVE INTO MY NEW PLACE... I am going to buy an Ultimate Dog bone. Regardless of the condition of the new dog bone. <P>Thanks again for the replies everyone.<P>WILLIAM... We really do need to meet up some time. I know my Fiero isn't as good as your awsome Fiero but, I'd really like to get a live look at it. Have you seen that sport coupe on 218? It was broke down on blanding one day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and everyone at Middleburg High was like " OHH Joey, What happened to the BEAST..."  haha  just cause of the colors being the same and not many fiero's around here. <BR> But give me an E-mail to meet up some time. I'd like that. <P>BroCar 87 ||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroSTETZ||06-12-2000||01:09 AM||||one thing i have noticed- on my 86SE (when the tranny worked) it would chirp on shifts, (4psd man) but my 87gt (with really squichy rubber ones) won't even make a peep on shifts. the 86 had not poly, but brand new rubber bushings. is the dog bone a factor here, or was that an ass o meter thing, or was that just because of the 4spd ratio? (always wondered why the 4spd pulls so much harder- the tires let go under hard aceleration if i go much higher than 5k rpm in second- i didnt know fieros did this- is this the gearing?)||||reg||1
Z||000014||87ECO5||06-12-2000||08:43 AM||||As Ogre said, you will get more vibration from the poly bushing TRS but YMMV on the amount of that vibration.<P>I'm running an '87 2.5 5-speed with the Ultimate and I'm now getting a severe amount of vibration.  Interior panels rattle and buzz like crazy.  You feel EVERYTHING the engine is doing.  It's harder to hold a conversation in the car now because the noise levels TRIPLED (well, not really but it's VERY loud in there)!<P>My suggestion is this:  find someone that has an Ultimate and borrow it from them for a few days ... or just take my advice.  If you're using the car as a daily driver and noise is something you'd rather not bring along for the ride, consider the OEM TRS.  It may wear out quicker, but, IMHO, that's better than having to tolerate the excessive amount of roughness that comes with the poly.<P>Just my $0.02 ...||||reg||1
Z||000015||BroCar 87||06-12-2000||05:39 PM||||Well I did my looking around and could only find the O.E.M. torque strut/mount for as cheap as $30 with a 2 day delivery time. The ULTIMATE dog bone was a total of $55 and a 2 day shipping time. <BR>So Tommorrow... I am ordering the Ultimate dogbone because, WHY waste money on something thats just about the same price that I will be replacing anyways, right.<BR>I will be a lot happier with it too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
